{"description": "Manifests and registers the retrieval model for a completed RAG ingestion, writes its governance artifacts, and generates the scheduled ingestion job from the Studio Flow that produced it.", "displayName": "RAG - Register Setup.step", "flowMetadata": {"inputPorts": [{"name": "_rgrg_inventory", "displayName": "_rgrg_inventory", "minEntries": 1, "maxEntries": 1, "type": "table", "id": "_rgrg_inventory", "label": "_rgrg_inventory"}], "outputPorts": [{"name": "_rgrg_report", "displayName": "_rgrg_report", "minEntries": 1, "maxEntries": 1, "columnDelta": null, "type": "table"}]}, "metadataVersion": 1, "name": "RAG - Register Setup.step", "properties": {}, "templates": {"SAS": "/******************************************************************************\n * Copyright \u00a9 2026, SAS Institute Inc., Cary, NC, USA.  All Rights Reserved.\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n *\n * RAG - Register Setup: turn a finished ingestion into something that can\n * be consumed and audited. Manifests retrieve_context.py for this setup and\n * registers it in SAS Model Manager as a scoreable python model, writes the\n * governance artifacts (pipeline.yaml, the ingestion and collection\n * manifests, the store DDL), and - when a Studio Flow is selected -\n * generates the scheduled ingestion job FROM that flow, so the job and the\n * flow cannot drift apart. Re-running updates in place.\n * Thin shell over rag_core.registration - see the About tab.\n ******************************************************************************/\n%macro _rgrg_setup;\n    %if not %symexist(_rgrg_ragProject) %then %global _rgrg_ragProject;\n    %if not %symexist(_rgrg_tablesCaslib) %then %global _rgrg_tablesCaslib;\n    /* The checkbox Verify TLS certificates in the registered retrieval model\n       arrives as 1 (ticked) or 0 (unticked). A flow that was saved before\n       the control existed, or a caller that sets nothing, leaves it missing\n       or blank - that reads as ticked, the safe value. */\n    %if not %symexist(_rgrg_sslVerify) %then %global _rgrg_sslVerify;\n    %if %length(%superq(_rgrg_sslVerify)) EQ 0 %then %let _rgrg_sslVerify = 1;\n%mend _rgrg_setup;\n%_rgrg_setup;\n/* Pipeline-wide state, shared by every RAG step in this session.\n   RAG_ABORT_ON_ERROR: 1 (default) stops a SAS Studio Flow at the failing\n   step, which is what an interactive user wants. A SCHEDULED run sets it to\n   0: an aborted session never sends SAS Job Execution its completion\n   handshake, so the job would report running forever and its dead compute\n   server would keep counting against the context's server limit.\n   RAG_PIPELINE_FAILED: set by the step that fails; later steps then skip\n   their work and pass the inventory through, so the flow finishes tidily\n   instead of loading half a corpus. A step that starts a chain (List\n   Documents, Purge Documents, Retrieve Context) clears it again.\n   RAG_JOB_FAILED: set by the step that fails as well, and cleared by no\n   step. A job generated from a flow tests it at its end: the flag above\n   may have been cleared by a later chain of the same flow by then. */\n%macro _rag_pipeline_state;\n    %if not %symexist(RAG_ABORT_ON_ERROR) %then %do;\n        %global RAG_ABORT_ON_ERROR;\n        %let RAG_ABORT_ON_ERROR = 1;\n    %end;\n    %if %length(%superq(RAG_ABORT_ON_ERROR)) EQ 0 %then\n        %let RAG_ABORT_ON_ERROR = 1;\n    %if not %symexist(RAG_PIPELINE_FAILED) %then %global RAG_PIPELINE_FAILED;\n    %if %length(%superq(RAG_PIPELINE_FAILED)) EQ 0 %then\n        %let RAG_PIPELINE_FAILED = 0;\n%mend _rag_pipeline_state;\n%_rag_pipeline_state;\n\n%let _rgrg_viyaHost = %sysfunc(getoption(SERVICESBASEURL));\n%let _rgrg_rc = 1;\n%let _rgrg_state = run;\n%let _rgrg_error = The Python program did not run.;\n%let _rgrg_summary = ;\n%let _rgrg_nrows = 0;\n/* What the STORED score code does about TLS certificates, set by the Python\n   below: on, off, or stale (verification was to be switched off, but the\n   deployed RAG content predates the setting, so the model still verifies).\n   _rgrg_tlsTag is failed when the tag TLS-Verification-Off could not be set\n   on the model or removed from it, and assumed when a run whose score code\n   is not known to be stored wrote the tag to a model it could not read.\n   Both are also set by a run that FAILS after the score code was stored:\n   the model then holds that code, whatever failed afterwards. unsure is\n   the state of a run whose upload of the score code got no usable answer:\n   the service may have stored the file, and the tag was not updated.\n   unknown stays for a run that did not get as far as the score code. */\n%let _rgrg_tlsState = unknown;\n%let _rgrg_tlsTag = ok;\n\n%macro _rgrg_guard;\n    %if &RAG_PIPELINE_FAILED. NE 0 %then %do;\n        %let _rgrg_state = skip;\n        data _null_;\n            putLog \"NOTE: RAG - Register Setup: skipped - an earlier step of this run failed\";\n        run;\n    %end;\n%mend _rgrg_guard;\n%_rgrg_guard;\n%macro _rgrg_inherit;\n    %global _rgrg_runId;\n    %local dsid vproject vcaslib vrun rc;\n    %if %symexist(_rgrg_inventory) %then\n    %if %length(%superq(_rgrg_inventory)) NE 0 %then %do;\n        %if %sysfunc(exist(&_rgrg_inventory.)) %then %do;\n            %let dsid = %sysfunc(open(&_rgrg_inventory., i));\n            %if &dsid. NE 0 %then %do;\n                %let vproject = %sysfunc(varnum(&dsid., rag_project));\n                %let vcaslib = %sysfunc(varnum(&dsid., tables_caslib));\n                %let vrun = %sysfunc(varnum(&dsid., run_id));\n                %if %sysfunc(fetch(&dsid.)) EQ 0 %then %do;\n                    %if &vproject. GT 0 %then\n                        %let _rgrg_ragProject = %sysfunc(getvarc(&dsid., &vproject.));\n                    %if &vcaslib. GT 0 %then\n                        %let _rgrg_tablesCaslib = %sysfunc(getvarc(&dsid., &vcaslib.));\n                    /* the run id too: the lock belongs to the RUN, so a step\n                       that fails has to know which lock row to hand back */\n                    %if &vrun. GT 0 %then\n                        %let _rgrg_runId = %sysfunc(getvarc(&dsid., &vrun.));\n                %end;\n                %let rc = %sysfunc(close(&dsid.));\n            %end;\n        %end;\n    %end;\n    /* a missing project is a failure of THIS step - but not when the step is\n       already skipping, where an absent inventory is expected */\n    %if &_rgrg_state. EQ run %then\n    %if %length(%superq(_rgrg_ragProject)) EQ 0 %then %do;\n        %let _rgrg_state = fail;\n        /* one line: the value is the message of the ERROR line below */\n        %let _rgrg_error = the inventory does not name a RAG project - wire the output of RAG - List Documents into this step;\n    %end;\n    %if %length(%superq(_rgrg_tablesCaslib)) EQ 0 %then\n        %let _rgrg_tablesCaslib = casuser;\n%mend _rgrg_inherit;\n%_rgrg_inherit;\n%macro _rgrg_port_default;\n    %if not %symexist(_rgrg_report) %then %global _rgrg_report;\n    %if %length(%superq(_rgrg_report)) EQ 0 %then\n        %let _rgrg_report = rgrgout.&_rgrg_ragProject._REGISTERED;\n%mend _rgrg_port_default;\n%_rgrg_port_default;\n\n/* One CAS session for the whole step: created here, reused by\n   SWAT inside proc python, promote+save done by proc casutil.\n   rgrgout is where the step's OUTPUT TABLE lands by default -\n   the same caslib as the pipeline tables, so a flow leaves its\n   intermediate results next to each other. */\ncas rgrgcas uuidmac=_rgrg_casuuid;\n%let _rgrg_cashost = %sysfunc(getoption(CASHOST));\n%let _rgrg_casport = %sysfunc(getoption(CASPORT));\nlibname rgrgout cas caslib=\"&_rgrg_tablesCaslib.\" sessref=rgrgcas;\n\n/* A pipeline table that was saved but is not in memory - which is how a CAS\n   server restart leaves every one of them - is loaded back before anything\n   looks at it. The code below only ever tests the in-memory table, so a\n   saved table that is not loaded would read as no previous run at all:\n   every document new, the whole corpus embedded again, and the saved file\n   overwritten by the result.\n   Nothing is done for a table that is in memory or was never saved. A saved\n   file that cannot be loaded FAILS the run, through the caller's state and\n   error variables, because carrying on would destroy what the file holds. */\n%macro _rag_reload_saved(sessref, caslib, table, statevar, errorvar);\n    %local _rag_reload_outcome _rag_reload_syscc;\n    %if %superq(&statevar.) NE run %then %return;\n    %let _rag_reload_outcome = unknown;\n    %let _rag_reload_syscc = &syscc.;\n    proc cas;\n        session &sessref.;\n        outcome = \"memory\";\n        table.tableExists result = found / caslib = \"&caslib.\" name = \"&table.\";\n        if found.exists == 0 then do;\n            /* The saved file carries the table name as it was typed and a\n               path-based caslib is case-sensitive, while CAS table names\n               are not - so the file is looked up in the listing: the exact\n               name when there is one, otherwise the same name in another\n               case. */\n            outcome = \"absent\";\n            saved = \"\";\n            table.fileInfo result = listing status = listed / caslib = \"&caslib.\";\n            if listed.severity == 0 then do;\n                if exists(listing, \"FileInfo\") then do;\n                    do entry over listing.FileInfo;\n                        if entry.Name == \"&table..sashdat\" then\n                            saved = entry.Name;\n                        else if saved == \"\" and upcase(entry.Name) == upcase(\"&table..sashdat\") then\n                            saved = entry.Name;\n                    end;\n                end;\n            end;\n            else outcome = \"unlisted\";\n            if saved != \"\" then do;\n                table.loadTable result = ignored status = loaded / caslib = \"&caslib.\" path = saved\n                    casOut = {caslib = \"&caslib.\", name = \"&table.\", promote = true};\n                /* A concurrent session may have loaded the table in the\n                   meantime. That refuses this load, and is just as good. */\n                table.tableExists result = found / caslib = \"&caslib.\" name = \"&table.\";\n                if found.exists != 0 then outcome = \"loaded\";\n                else outcome = \"failed\";\n            end;\n        end;\n        /* \"L\": the macro variable is local to this macro, and without a\n           scope CASL writes to the global symbol table */\n        call symputx(\"_rag_reload_outcome\", outcome, \"L\");\n    quit;\n    /* Looking is not part of the run and never decides its condition code:\n       not a load that was refused because another session got there first,\n       and not a load that failed either - that one is reported through the\n       caller's state, the way the caller reports every other failure. */\n    %let syscc = &_rag_reload_syscc.;\n    %if &_rag_reload_outcome. EQ failed %then %do;\n        %let &statevar. = fail;\n        /* one line: the caller writes it to the log as its ERROR line */\n        %let &errorvar. = the saved table &caslib..&table. could not be loaded into memory (CAS messages above) - stopped, because an empty table would re-embed the corpus and overwrite the saved file;\n        %return;\n    %end;\n    /* The run goes on in the two cases that are left, and says what that\n       means. unlisted: the table is not in memory and the files of the caslib\n       could not be listed, so no saved copy was looked for - the case the\n       reload is there for, without the reload. Anything else: PROC CAS ended\n       before it handed back an outcome, and not even that much is known. */\n    %if &_rag_reload_outcome. EQ loaded %then\n        %put NOTE: RAG: &caslib..&table. was saved but not in memory and has been loaded from its saved file.;\n    %else %if &_rag_reload_outcome. EQ unlisted %then %do;\n        %put WARNING: RAG: &caslib..&table. is not in memory, and the files of the caslib &caslib. could not be listed (CAS messages above) - a saved copy could not be looked for.;\n        %put WARNING: RAG: the run continues without the table and saves over a copy that may be there. A ledger that is not in memory means that every document counts as new and is embedded again.;\n    %end;\n    %else %if &_rag_reload_outcome. NE memory and &_rag_reload_outcome. NE absent %then %do;\n        %put WARNING: RAG: could not look for &caslib..&table. - PROC CAS ended before it said whether the table is in memory or saved (messages above). The run continues with what is in memory.;\n        %put WARNING: RAG: if the table is not in memory, the run saves over a copy that may be there. A ledger that is not in memory means that every document counts as new and is embedded again.;\n    %end;\n%mend _rag_reload_saved;\n%_rag_reload_saved(rgrgcas, &_rgrg_tablesCaslib., &_rgrg_ragProject._LEDGER, _rgrg_state, _rgrg_error);\n\n%macro _rgrg_export(portvar, file);\n    %if %symexist(&portvar.) %then %do;\n        %if %length(%superq(&&portvar.)) GT 0 %then %do;\n            %if %sysfunc(exist(&&&portvar..)) %then %do;\n                filename _rgrg_io \"%sysfunc(pathname(work))/&file.\";\n                proc json out=_rgrg_io noSASTags;\n                    export &&&portvar..;\n                run; quit;\n                filename _rgrg_io clear;\n            %end;\n        %end;\n    %end;\n%mend _rgrg_export;\n%_rgrg_export(_rgrg_inventory, rgrg_inventory_in.json);\n\nproc python restart;\nsubmit;\ndef main():\n    import json\n    import os\n    import sys\n    import tempfile\n    import time\n    import traceback\n\n    # nothing to do when the step is only passing the inventory through\n    if str(SAS.symget(\"_rgrg_state\") or \"run\").strip() != \"run\":\n        return\n\n    def sas_safe(text):\n        \"\"\"Strings crossing into SAS.logMessage/SAS.symput are embedded into\n        generated SAS statements - quotes and macro characters corrupt the\n        code stream (verified live). EVERY such string goes through here.\"\"\"\n        cleaned = str(text)\n        for ch in (\"'\", '\"', \"%\", \"&\", \";\"):\n            cleaned = cleaned.replace(ch, \" \")\n        return cleaned\n\n    def M(msg):\n        SAS.logMessage(\"RAGREGISTER \" + sas_safe(msg))\n\n    try:\n        import requests\n    except Exception:\n        SAS.symput(\"_rgrg_error\", \"The Python environment of this compute \"\n                                   \"context lacks the requests package - see \"\n                                   \"the RAG administration guide.\")\n        return\n    try:\n        import pandas as pd\n        import swat\n    except Exception:\n        SAS.symput(\"_rgrg_error\", \"The Python environment of this compute \"\n                                   \"context lacks the swat/pandas packages \"\n                                   \"required for the CAS table transport - \"\n                                   \"see the RAG administration guide.\")\n        return\n\n    BASE = str(SAS.symget(\"_rgrg_viyaHost\") or \"\").rstrip(\"/\")\n    TOKEN = os.environ.get(\"SAS_SERVICES_TOKEN\", \"\")\n    AUTH = {\"Authorization\": \"Bearer \" + TOKEN}\n    VERIFY = os.environ.get(\"SSLCALISTLOC\") or os.environ.get(\"CAS_CLIENT_SSL_CA_LIST\") or True\n    WORKPATH = SAS.workpath if SAS.workpath.endswith(os.sep) else SAS.workpath + os.sep\n\n    P = {name: str(SAS.symget(name) or \"\").strip() for name in [\n        \"_rgrg_setupName\",\n        \"_rgrg_storeHost\",\n        \"_rgrg_storePort\",\n        \"_rgrg_storeDb\",\n        \"_rgrg_storeSslmode\",\n        \"_rgrg_credentialDomain\",\n        \"_rgrg_scrEndpoint\",\n        \"_rgrg_defaultK\",\n        \"_rgrg_mmProject\",\n        \"_rgrg_casServer\",\n        \"_rgrg_flowPath\",\n        \"_rgrg_computeContext\",\n        \"_rgrg_contentRoot\",\n        \"_rgrg_modelTemplate\",\n        \"_rgrg_ragProject\",\n        \"_rgrg_tablesCaslib\",\n        \"_rgrg_ragCorePath\",\n    ]}\n\n    def verify_requested():\n        \"\"\"The checkbox Verify TLS certificates in the registered retrieval\n        model: False only for an explicit off value.\"\"\"\n        # SAS Studio hands a checkbox over as 1 (ticked) or 0 (unticked).\n        # Only an explicit off value switches verification off: a value\n        # that reads as the number zero (0, 0.0, 00, -0, 0e0), or the word\n        # false or no in any case. A blank, a missing or an unknown value -\n        # nan among them - keeps it on, so every way of misreading the\n        # control fails in the safe direction.\n        try:\n            raw = SAS.symget(\"_rgrg_sslVerify\")\n        except Exception:\n            raw = \"\"\n        word = \"\" if raw is None else str(raw).strip().lower()\n        try:\n            return float(word) != 0\n        except ValueError:\n            return word not in (\"false\", \"no\")\n\n    TLS_VERIFY = verify_requested()\n\n    def read_rows(filename, missing_message):\n        path = WORKPATH + filename\n        if not os.path.exists(path):\n            raise RuntimeError(missing_message)\n        with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:\n            data = json.load(fh)\n        rows = []\n        for row in data if isinstance(data, list) else []:\n            rows.append({str(k).lower(): v for k, v in row.items()})\n        return rows\n\n    def multiline(control):\n        \"\"\"Every line a user typed into a multi-line text field.\"\"\"\n        # SAS Studio splits such a field for us: it emits <control>_count and\n        # <control>_1..N, and leaves the plain macro variable holding only the\n        # FIRST line. Reading just the plain one silently turned two questions\n        # into one run-on question (found live in a flow). Semicolons are still\n        # accepted, for callers that set the parameter directly.\n        values = []\n        try:\n            count = int(float(SAS.symget(control + \"_count\") or 0))\n        except Exception:\n            count = 0\n        if count > 0:\n            for index in range(1, count + 1):\n                try:\n                    piece = str(SAS.symget(\"%s_%d\" % (control, index)) or \"\")\n                except Exception:\n                    piece = \"\"\n                if piece.strip():\n                    values.append(piece.strip())\n            if values:\n                return values\n        raw = str(P.get(control) or \"\").replace(\";\", \"\\n\")\n        return [line.strip() for line in raw.split(\"\\n\") if line.strip()]\n\n    def clean_path(raw):\n        \"\"\"Path-selector values arrive scheme-prefixed (sasserver:/...,\n        sascontent:/...); strip the scheme off.\"\"\"\n        value = str(raw or \"\").strip()\n        for scheme in (\"sascontent:\", \"sasserver:\"):\n            if value.lower().startswith(scheme):\n                return value[len(scheme):]\n        return value\n\n    STARTED = time.time()\n    SUMMARY = []\n\n    def summarize(line):\n        \"\"\"One line of the step's log summary (SAS prints them at the end).\"\"\"\n        SUMMARY.append(str(line))\n\n    def publish_summary(target):\n        elapsed = time.time() - STARTED\n        summarize(f\"elapsed {elapsed:.1f}s\")\n        SAS.symput(target, sas_safe(\" | \".join(SUMMARY))[:1500])\n\n    def write_rows(filename, rows, columns, numeric=()):\n        out = []\n        for row in rows:\n            rec = {}\n            for column in columns:\n                value = row.get(column)\n                if column in numeric:\n                    try:\n                        rec[column] = float(value or 0)\n                    except Exception:\n                        rec[column] = 0.0\n                else:\n                    rec[column] = \"\" if value is None else str(value)\n            out.append(rec)\n        with open(WORKPATH + filename, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:\n            json.dump(out, fh)\n        return len(out)\n\n    def tls_outcome(outcome):\n        \"\"\"Hand SAS what the STORED score code does; return it as a text.\"\"\"\n        # `outcome` is what register_setup read back from the manifested\n        # text: its result, or - for a run that failed after the score code\n        # was stored - what it put on the exception. A rag_core deployed\n        # before the setting existed returns none of these keys and writes\n        # no SSL_VERIFY line: such a model verifies, whatever the checkbox\n        # says.\n        tls_verifies = outcome.get('ssl_verify', True) is not False\n        tls_tag_failed = bool(outcome.get('tls_tag_error'))\n        if not tls_verifies:\n            tls_state = 'off'\n            tls_detail = ('TLS certificate verification OFF ('\n                          + ('the tag TLS-Verification-Off could not be written'\n                             if tls_tag_failed else 'tag TLS-Verification-Off')\n                          + ')')\n        elif not TLS_VERIFY:\n            tls_state = 'stale'\n            tls_detail = ('TLS certificate verification still ON - '\n                          + ('the retrieval model template'\n                             if 'ssl_verify' in outcome else 'the deployed rag_core')\n                          + ' predates the setting, deploy the RAG content again')\n        else:\n            tls_state = 'on'\n            tls_detail = 'TLS certificate verification on'\n        if tls_verifies and tls_tag_failed:\n            tls_detail += ' (the tag TLS-Verification-Off could not be removed)'\n        SAS.symput('_rgrg_tlsState', tls_state)\n        SAS.symput('_rgrg_tlsTag', 'failed' if tls_tag_failed else 'ok')\n        return tls_detail\n\n    try:\n        # ---- CAS: reuse the session the step created in SAS ---------------\n        # (sas-studio-custom-steps: Reuse-CAS-session-from-SWAT)\n        import re as _re\n        os.environ.setdefault(\"CAS_CLIENT_SSL_CA_LIST\",\n                              os.environ.get(\"SSLCALISTLOC\", \"\"))\n        try:\n            conn = swat.CAS(hostname=str(SAS.symget(\"_rgrg_cashost\") or \"\"),\n                            port=int(float(SAS.symget(\"_rgrg_casport\") or 5570)),\n                            password=TOKEN,\n                            session=str(SAS.symget(\"_rgrg_casuuid\") or \"\"))\n        except Exception as exc:\n            # The step reuses the CAS session SAS created, because the staged\n            # table has to be visible to the casutil promote that follows. CAS\n            # only lets an identity reconnect to its OWN session, and a context\n            # that runs the server as a service account breaks that: SAS and\n            # its token are the service account while the CAS session belongs\n            # to the user who launched the job.\n            #\n            # SWAT's exception says only \"Could not connect ... on port 5570\";\n            # the server's real message (\"Users can only reconnect to their own\n            # sessions\") goes to stderr and never reaches the exception, so\n            # matching on text does not work. Connecting WITHOUT the session id\n            # separates the two causes: if that works, CAS is reachable and the\n            # problem is whose session it is.\n            reachable = False\n            try:\n                probe = swat.CAS(\n                    hostname=str(SAS.symget(\"_rgrg_cashost\") or \"\"),\n                    port=int(float(SAS.symget(\"_rgrg_casport\") or 5570)),\n                    password=TOKEN)\n                reachable = True\n                probe.close()\n            except Exception:\n                pass\n            if reachable:\n                raise RuntimeError(\n                    \"this compute context cannot run the RAG steps: CAS is \"\n                    \"reachable, but the SAS session and the CAS session belong \"\n                    \"to different identities, so the step cannot reuse the CAS \"\n                    \"session it needs. The stock 'SAS Job Execution compute \"\n                    \"context' has this problem because it runs the server as a \"\n                    \"service account. Run the job in a context that runs as the \"\n                    \"REQUESTING USER - the 'SAS Studio compute context' does, \"\n                    \"and a full flow was verified there. See the RAG \"\n                    \"administration guide.\")\n            raise\n        CASLIB = P[\"_rgrg_tablesCaslib\"] or \"casuser\"\n        if not _re.match(r\"^[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_]{0,19}$\",\n                         P[\"_rgrg_ragProject\"] or \"\"):\n            raise RuntimeError(\n                \"ragProject must be 1-20 characters (letters, digits, \"\n                \"underscores, starting with a letter) so every \"\n                \"project_suffix table name stays within the 32 characters \"\n                \"SAS Studio displays\")\n\n        def project_table(suffix):\n            return P[\"_rgrg_ragProject\"] + suffix\n\n        def stamp(rows):\n            \"\"\"Every inventory row names its pipeline, so the next step\n            inherits the project and caslib instead of asking again.\"\"\"\n            for row in rows:\n                row[\"rag_project\"] = P[\"_rgrg_ragProject\"]\n                row[\"tables_caslib\"] = CASLIB\n            return rows\n\n        def cas_read(name, required_message=None):\n            \"\"\"Read a pipeline table into lower-cased row dicts; absent\n            table = empty (the pipeline's empty state) unless required.\"\"\"\n            if not conn.table.tableExists(caslib=CASLIB, name=name).exists:\n                if required_message:\n                    raise RuntimeError(required_message)\n                return []\n            frame = conn.CASTable(name, caslib=CASLIB).to_frame()\n            rows = []\n            for record in frame.to_dict(\"records\"):\n                row = {}\n                for key, value in record.items():\n                    row[str(key).lower()] = None if pd.isna(value) else value\n                rows.append(row)\n            return rows\n\n        def ledger_value(value):\n            \"\"\"One value of a ledger row, as the pipeline compares it.\"\"\"\n            # The text columns of the ledger are VARCHAR when the Load step\n            # wrote it and CHAR when the single-program job did, and CAS\n            # stores a CHAR value padded with blanks to the length of its\n            # column. Whether SWAT hands that padding on was not measured,\n            # so it is taken off here: a padded run id is not the id of\n            # this run, and a padded fingerprint is not the fingerprint of\n            # the document.\n            if value is None:\n                return \"\"\n            if isinstance(value, str):\n                return value.rstrip(\" \")\n            return value\n\n        def label_columns(name, columns):\n            \"\"\"Put the shipped column labels on a CAS table - they survive\n            the promote, so the pipeline tables read without the schema.\"\"\"\n            try:\n                from rag_core.steps import column_labels\n                labels = column_labels(columns)\n                if labels:\n                    conn.table.alterTable(\n                        caslib=CASLIB, name=name,\n                        columns=[{\"name\": column, \"label\": label}\n                                 for column, label in labels.items()])\n            except Exception as exc:\n                M(f\"column labels not applied to {name}: {exc}\")\n\n        def cas_stage(name, rows, columns, numeric=()):\n            \"\"\"Upload the session-scope staging table <name>_S with varchar\n            columns (no 32k limit); the SAS side swaps it into the promoted\n            global table and saves it, so the previous state survives a\n            mid-step failure.\"\"\"\n            if not rows:\n                return 0\n            data = []\n            for row in rows:\n                rec = []\n                for column in columns:\n                    value = row.get(column)\n                    if column in numeric:\n                        try:\n                            rec.append(float(value or 0))\n                        except Exception:\n                            rec.append(0.0)\n                    else:\n                        rec.append(\"\" if value is None else str(value))\n                data.append(rec)\n            frame = pd.DataFrame(data, columns=list(columns))\n            spec = [{\"name\": column,\n                     \"type\": \"double\" if column in numeric else \"varchar\"}\n                    for column in columns]\n            conn.upload_frame(frame,\n                              casout={\"name\": name + \"_S\", \"caslib\": CASLIB,\n                                      \"replace\": True},\n                              importoptions={\"fileType\": \"csv\",\n                                             \"allowEmbeddedNewLines\": True,\n                                             \"vars\": spec})\n            label_columns(name + \"_S\", columns)\n            return len(rows)\n\n        # ---- rag_core bootstrap: download the governed SAS Content folder --\n        def get_json(endpoint, **params):\n            response = requests.get(BASE + endpoint, params=params, headers=AUTH,\n                                    verify=VERIFY, timeout=(5, 30))\n            response.raise_for_status()\n            return response.json()\n\n        def download_folder(folder_id, local_dir):\n            os.makedirs(local_dir, exist_ok=True)\n            count = 0\n            members = get_json(f\"/folders/folders/{folder_id}/members\", limit=200)\n            for member in members.get(\"items\", []):\n                uri = member.get(\"uri\", \"\")\n                if \"/files/files/\" in uri:\n                    content = requests.get(BASE + uri + \"/content\", headers=AUTH,\n                                           verify=VERIFY, timeout=(5, 60))\n                    content.raise_for_status()\n                    with open(os.path.join(local_dir, member[\"name\"]), \"wb\") as fh:\n                        fh.write(content.content)\n                    count += 1\n                elif \"/folders/folders/\" in uri:\n                    count += download_folder(uri.rsplit(\"/\", 1)[-1],\n                                             os.path.join(local_dir, member[\"name\"]))\n            return count\n\n        core_path = (clean_path(P[\"_rgrg_ragCorePath\"])\n                     or \"/SAS Agentic AI Accelerator/RAG/rag_core\")\n        root = requests.get(BASE + \"/folders/folders/@item\",\n                            params={\"path\": core_path}, headers=AUTH,\n                            verify=VERIFY, timeout=(5, 30))\n        if root.status_code != 200:\n            raise RuntimeError(f\"rag_core folder {core_path} not found \"\n                               f\"(HTTP {root.status_code}) - deploy it per the \"\n                               \"administration guide\")\n        staging = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=\"rag_core_\")\n        n_files = download_folder(root.json()[\"id\"], os.path.join(staging, \"rag_core\"))\n        sys.path.insert(0, staging)\n        import rag_core\n        M(f\"rag_core {rag_core.RAG_CORE_VERSION} bootstrapped ({n_files} files)\")\n\n        from rag_core.adapters import get_adapter\n        from rag_core.credentials import fetch_secrets, store_config_from_secrets\n        from rag_core.env import default_port\n        from rag_core.manifest import settings_from_inventory\n        from rag_core.registration import ViyaClient, register_setup\n        from rag_core.steps import LEDGER_COLUMNS\n\n        setup = P[\"_rgrg_setupName\"]\n        if not setup:\n            raise RuntimeError('give the setup a name - it names the model, '\n                               'the generated job and the artifact folder')\n        inventory = read_rows('rgrg_inventory_in.json',\n                              'the inventory input port is not connected - '\n                              'wire the RAG - Load Vector Store report into '\n                              'this step')\n        ledger = []\n        for row in cas_read(project_table('_LEDGER')):\n            ledger.append({column: ledger_value(row.get(column))\n                           for column in LEDGER_COLUMNS})\n\n        settings = settings_from_inventory(inventory, {\n            'setup': setup,\n            'STORE_HOST': P[\"_rgrg_storeHost\"],\n            'STORE_PORT': P[\"_rgrg_storePort\"],\n            'STORE_DB': P[\"_rgrg_storeDb\"],\n            'STORE_SSLMODE': P[\"_rgrg_storeSslmode\"] or 'prefer',\n            'CREDENTIAL_DOMAIN': P[\"_rgrg_credentialDomain\"] or 'agentic-ai-keys',\n            'EMBED_ENDPOINT': P[\"_rgrg_scrEndpoint\"] or (BASE + '/llm'),\n            'DEFAULT_K': int(float(P[\"_rgrg_defaultK\"] or 4)),\n            # the literal False is the only value that writes SSL_VERIFY =\n            # False; rag_core.manifest writes True for everything else\n            'SSL_VERIFY': TLS_VERIFY,\n        })\n        if not TLS_VERIFY:\n            M('the checkbox Verify TLS certificates in the registered '\n              'retrieval model is unticked - registering with verification '\n              'switched off')\n        for required in ('COLLECTION', 'BACKEND', 'EMBED_MODEL'):\n            if not settings.get(required):\n                raise RuntimeError(\n                    'the inventory does not carry ' + required.lower()\n                    + ' - run this step after RAG - Load Vector Store, whose '\n                      'report records what was loaded where')\n\n        # the backend comes from the inventory, not from a control here, so\n        # the port default can only be applied once it is known\n        if not settings.get('STORE_PORT'):\n            settings['STORE_PORT'] = str(default_port(settings['BACKEND']))\n\n        # the collection itself answers for its width and its DDL; nothing in\n        # the flow carries dimensions, by design\n        ddl = ''\n        live_chunks = -1\n        try:\n            secrets = fetch_secrets(BASE, TOKEN, settings['CREDENTIAL_DOMAIN'],\n                                    verify=VERIFY)\n            adapter = get_adapter(settings['BACKEND'])\n            adapter.connect(store_config_from_secrets(\n                secrets, settings['BACKEND'], settings['STORE_HOST'],\n                settings['STORE_PORT'], settings['STORE_DB'],\n                settings['STORE_SSLMODE']))\n            dims = adapter.dimensions(settings['COLLECTION'])\n            settings['dims'] = dims\n            if dims:\n                ddl = adapter.ddl(settings['COLLECTION'], dims)\n            live_chunks = adapter.count(settings['COLLECTION'])\n            adapter.close()\n        except Exception as exc:\n            # registration is still worth doing without the store artifacts\n            M('the vector store could not be read for the DDL artifact: '\n              + str(exc)[:200])\n\n        template_path = clean_path(P[\"_rgrg_modelTemplate\"])\n        template = ''\n        if template_path:\n            folder_path, _, wanted = template_path.rpartition('/')\n            found = requests.get(BASE + '/folders/folders/@item',\n                                 params={'path': folder_path}, headers=AUTH,\n                                 verify=VERIFY, timeout=(5, 30))\n            if found.status_code == 200:\n                members = get_json('/folders/folders/%s/members'\n                                   % found.json()['id'], limit=200)\n                for member in members.get('items', []):\n                    if member.get('name') == wanted:\n                        got = requests.get(BASE + member['uri'] + '/content',\n                                           headers=AUTH, verify=VERIFY,\n                                           timeout=(5, 60))\n                        got.raise_for_status()\n                        template = got.text\n                        break\n        if not template:\n            raise RuntimeError('the retrieval model template was not found at '\n                               + str(template_path) + ' - deploy the RAG '\n                               'content bundle first')\n\n        client = ViyaClient(BASE, TOKEN, verify=VERIFY)\n        outcome = register_setup(\n            client, settings, template, ledger,\n            content_root=clean_path(P[\"_rgrg_contentRoot\"]),\n            setup_name=setup,\n            mm_project=P[\"_rgrg_mmProject\"] or 'RAG Engineering',\n            ddl=ddl, cas_server=P[\"_rgrg_casServer\"] or 'cas-shared-default',\n            flow_path=clean_path(P[\"_rgrg_flowPath\"]),\n            compute_context=P[\"_rgrg_computeContext\"], log=M)\n\n        # What the STORED score code does, as register_setup read it back\n        # from the manifested text.\n        tls_detail = tls_outcome(outcome)\n\n        rows = [{'registered': 'model', 'name': outcome['model_name'],\n                 'location': '/modelRepository/models/' + outcome['model_id'],\n                 'detail': 'scoreable python model, score file manifested, '\n                           + tls_detail}]\n        for artifact in outcome['artifacts']:\n            rows.append({'registered': 'artifact', 'name': artifact,\n                         'location': outcome['folder'], 'detail': ''})\n        if outcome.get('job_id'):\n            rows.append({'registered': 'job', 'name': outcome['job_name'],\n                         'location': '/jobDefinitions/definitions/'\n                                     + outcome['job_id'],\n                         'detail': 'generated from '\n                                   + str(outcome.get('flow') or '')})\n        n_rows = write_rows('rgrg_report_out.json', rows,\n                            ['registered', 'name', 'location', 'detail'])\n        SAS.symput('_rgrg_nrows', str(n_rows))\n\n        summarize('setup ' + setup)\n        summarize('collection %s in %s (%s dimensions)'\n                  % (settings['COLLECTION'], settings['BACKEND'],\n                     settings.get('dims') or 'unknown'))\n        if live_chunks >= 0:\n            summarize('%d live chunks in the collection' % live_chunks)\n        summarize('retrieval model ' + outcome['model_name'] + ' registered in '\n                  + (P[\"_rgrg_mmProject\"] or 'RAG Engineering'))\n        summarize('artifacts in ' + outcome['folder'] + ': '\n                  + ', '.join(outcome['artifacts']))\n        if outcome.get('job_id'):\n            summarize('scheduled job ' + outcome['job_name']\n                      + ' generated from the flow - schedule it in SAS '\n                        'Environment Manager')\n        else:\n            summarize('no flow selected, so no scheduled job was generated')\n        summarize('corpus version stamped into the model: '\n                  + str(settings.get('INGESTION_RUN_ID') or 'none'))\n        summarize('retrieval model: ' + tls_detail)\n        publish_summary('_rgrg_summary')\n\n        try:\n            conn.close(close_session=False)\n        except Exception:\n            pass\n        SAS.symput(\"_rgrg_rc\", \"0\")\n    except Exception as error:\n        error_text = f\"{type(error).__name__}: {error}\"\n        M(\"failed: \" + sas_safe(error_text))\n        print(traceback.format_exc())\n        SAS.symput(\"_rgrg_error\", sas_safe(error_text)[:500])\n        # A registration that failed on the way says how far it got: rag_core\n        # puts `registration` on the exception once the model exists (an\n        # older rag_core puts nothing there, and the state stays unknown).\n        # A model whose score code was stored holds that code, whatever\n        # failed afterwards - a flow that does not exist, say - so the step\n        # says what it does about TLS certificates in this run as well. An\n        # upload without a usable answer is said as what it is: not known.\n        reached = getattr(error, \"registration\", None)\n        if isinstance(reached, dict):\n            stored = str(reached.get(\"score_code\") or \"\")\n            if stored == \"stored\":\n                M(\"the step failed after the score code was stored - \"\n                  \"retrieval model: \" + tls_outcome(reached))\n            elif stored == \"unknown\":\n                SAS.symput('_rgrg_tlsState', 'unsure')\n                M(\"it is not known whether the score code was stored - the \"\n                  \"tag TLS-Verification-Off may not say what the model does\")\n            # The model could not be read before it was updated and the\n            # listing did not show its tags: rag_core then WRITES the tag.\n            # Once the score code is stored the tag is settled after it; in\n            # a run that did not get there, the tag is one this run put on\n            # the model, and the step says so.\n            if stored != \"stored\" and reached.get(\"tls_tag_assumed\") is True:\n                SAS.symput('_rgrg_tlsTag', 'assumed')\n                M(\"the model could not be read before it was updated - the \"\n                  \"tag TLS-Verification-Off was written to it unseen\")\n\n\nmain()\nendsubmit;\nrun; quit;\nproc python terminate;\nrun; quit;\n\n%macro _rgrg_emit_report;\n    %if &_rgrg_rc. NE 0 %then %return;\n    %local lib table opts;\n    %let lib = %upcase(%scan(&_rgrg_report., 1, .));\n    %let table = %scan(&_rgrg_report., 2, .);\n    %if &lib. EQ %upcase(rgrgout) %then %do;\n        proc casutil sessref=rgrgcas\n                     incaslib=\"&_rgrg_tablesCaslib.\"\n                     outcaslib=\"&_rgrg_tablesCaslib.\";\n            droptable casdata=\"&table.\" quiet;\n        quit;\n        %let opts = (promote=yes);\n    %end;\n    %else %let opts = (compress=yes);\n    %if &_rgrg_nrows. GT 0 %then %do;\n        filename rgrgreo \"%sysfunc(pathname(work))/rgrg_report_out.json\";\n        libname rgrgrej json fileref=rgrgreo;\n        data &_rgrg_report.&opts.;\n            length registered $ 16 name $ 128 location $ 512 detail $ 256;\n            label registered=\"Registered item\" name=\"Name\" location=\"Location\"\n                  detail=\"Detail\";\n            set rgrgrej.root(drop=ordinal_root);\n        run;\n        libname rgrgrej clear;\n        filename rgrgreo clear;\n    %end;\n    %else %do;\n        data &_rgrg_report.&opts.;\n            length registered $ 16 name $ 128 location $ 512 detail $ 256;\n            label registered=\"Registered item\" name=\"Name\" location=\"Location\"\n                  detail=\"Detail\";\n            call missing(of _all_);\n            stop;\n        run;\n    %end;\n%mend _rgrg_emit_report;\n%_rgrg_emit_report;\n%macro _rgrg_release;\n    %local failing held;\n    %let failing = 0;\n    %if &_rgrg_state. EQ fail %then %let failing = 1;\n    %if &_rgrg_state. EQ run %then %if &_rgrg_rc. NE 0 %then %let failing = 1;\n    %if &failing. EQ 0 %then %return;\n    %if not %symexist(_rgrg_runId) %then %return;\n    %if %length(%superq(_rgrg_runId)) EQ 0 %then %return;\n    %if not %sysfunc(exist(rgrgout.&_rgrg_ragProject._LEDGER)) %then %return;\n    /* Only a run whose own lock row stands in the ledger has a lock to hand\n       back. A run that the fresh lock of another run refused took none, a\n       preview of RAG - Purge Documents takes none, and the row is gone once\n       the run has written its ledger (RAG - Load Vector Store, or a purge).\n       Rewriting the ledger then released nothing: it saved the table again\n       - with the lock of the OTHER run in the file that is loaded back when\n       the table is no longer in memory - and the NOTE below said that a\n       lock had been released. */\n    %let held = ;\n    data _null_;\n        set rgrgout.&_rgrg_ragProject._LEDGER(where=(doc_id = \"__run_lock__\" and run_id = \"&_rgrg_runId.\"));\n        call symputx(\"held\", run_id, \"L\");\n    run;\n    %if %length(&held.) EQ 0 %then %return;\n    data rgrgout.&_rgrg_ragProject._LEDGER_R(replace=yes);\n        set rgrgout.&_rgrg_ragProject._LEDGER(where=(not (doc_id = \"__run_lock__\"\n                                 and run_id = \"&_rgrg_runId.\")));\n    run;\n    proc casutil sessref=rgrgcas incaslib=\"&_rgrg_tablesCaslib.\"\n                 outcaslib=\"&_rgrg_tablesCaslib.\";\n        droptable casdata=\"&_rgrg_ragProject._LEDGER\" quiet;\n        promote casdata=\"&_rgrg_ragProject._LEDGER_R\"\n                casout=\"&_rgrg_ragProject._LEDGER\";\n        save casdata=\"&_rgrg_ragProject._LEDGER\"\n             casout=\"&_rgrg_ragProject._LEDGER\" replace;\n    quit;\n    data _null_;\n        putLog \"NOTE: RAG - Register Setup: the run lock was released so the run can be retried\";\n    run;\n%mend _rgrg_release;\n%_rgrg_release;\n\nlibname rgrgout clear;\ncas rgrgcas terminate;\n\n/* TLS certificate verification, said as WARNING lines so that a model\n   that does not verify cannot be registered unnoticed. The lines describe\n   the model as SAS Model Manager holds it, so they are written by a run\n   that went through and by one that failed after the score code was\n   stored. Every literal stays below 262 characters, the length at which\n   SAS starts to suspect an unbalanced quotation mark. */\n%macro _rgrg_tls_warnings;\n    %if &_rgrg_tlsState. EQ off %then %do;\n        data _null_;\n            putLog \"WARNING: RAG - Register Setup: this retrieval model does NOT verify TLS certificates. Its two HTTPS calls - to the embedding container and to the SAS Viya credentials service - accept any certificate.\";\n            putLog \"WARNING: RAG - Register Setup: to turn verification back on where the model runs, set RAGEMBED_SSLVERIFY=true and RAGSTORE_SSLVERIFY=true on the publishing destination.\";\n            putLog \"WARNING: RAG - Register Setup: to register a model that verifies, tick the checkbox Verify TLS certificates in the registered retrieval model (Runtime section) and run this step again.\";\n        run;\n        %if &_rgrg_tlsTag. EQ failed %then %do;\n            data _null_;\n                putLog \"WARNING: RAG - Register Setup: the tag TLS-Verification-Off could not be written to the model. Add the tag in SAS Model Manager, so that the model can be found as one that does not verify.\";\n            run;\n        %end;\n        %else %do;\n            data _null_;\n                putLog \"WARNING: RAG - Register Setup: the model carries the tag TLS-Verification-Off in SAS Model Manager.\";\n            run;\n        %end;\n    %end;\n    %else %do;\n        %if &_rgrg_tlsState. EQ stale %then %do;\n            data _null_;\n                putLog \"WARNING: RAG - Register Setup: TLS certificate verification is still ON in this retrieval model, although the checkbox Verify TLS certificates in the registered retrieval model is unticked.\";\n                putLog \"WARNING: RAG - Register Setup: the deployed RAG content predates the setting - the retrieval model template has no SSL_VERIFY line, or rag_core does not write it.\";\n                putLog \"WARNING: RAG - Register Setup: deploy the RAG content again (deploy-rag-content) and run this step once more for the setting to take effect.\";\n            run;\n        %end;\n        %if &_rgrg_tlsState. EQ unsure %then %do;\n            data _null_;\n                putLog \"WARNING: RAG - Register Setup: it is not known whether SAS Model Manager stored the score code retrieve_context.py. The upload got no usable answer, and the file may have been stored all the same.\";\n            run;\n            /* The tag is settled after the upload, and this run did not get\n               there. Where the run wrote the tag to a model it could not\n               read, it did so BEFORE the upload, and the lines below say\n               that: this one then says after the upload, as rag_core does -\n               it said that the tag was not updated, and the next line that\n               the run had written it. */\n            %if &_rgrg_tlsTag. EQ assumed %then %do;\n                data _null_;\n                    putLog \"WARNING: RAG - Register Setup: the tag TLS-Verification-Off was not updated after the upload and may not say what the stored score code does. Run this step again.\";\n                run;\n            %end;\n            %else %do;\n                data _null_;\n                    putLog \"WARNING: RAG - Register Setup: the tag TLS-Verification-Off was not updated and may not say what the stored score code does. Run this step again.\";\n                run;\n            %end;\n        %end;\n        /* A run that did not store its score code, or does not know whether\n           it did, on a model it could not read and whose tags the listing\n           did not show: the update before the upload wrote the tag. */\n        %if &_rgrg_tlsTag. EQ assumed %then %do;\n            data _null_;\n                putLog \"WARNING: RAG - Register Setup: the model could not be read before this run updated it, and the listing of the models did not show its tags.\";\n                putLog \"WARNING: RAG - Register Setup: before the upload the run therefore wrote the tag TLS-Verification-Off to the model, without knowing whether the model carried it.\";\n                putLog \"WARNING: RAG - Register Setup: the score code of this run was not stored, or it is not known whether it was, so the tag may not say what the model does. Run this step again.\";\n            run;\n        %end;\n        %if &_rgrg_tlsTag. EQ failed %then %do;\n            data _null_;\n                putLog \"WARNING: RAG - Register Setup: the tag TLS-Verification-Off could not be removed from the model. This retrieval model verifies TLS: if the model still carries the tag, remove it in SAS Model Manager.\";\n            run;\n        %end;\n    %end;\n%mend _rgrg_tls_warnings;\n\n%macro _rgrg_status;\n    %local stored;\n    %if &_rgrg_state. EQ run %then %if &_rgrg_rc. NE 0 %then\n        %let _rgrg_state = fail;\n    %if &_rgrg_state. EQ skip %then %do;\n        data _null_;\n            putLog \"NOTE: ----- RAG - Register Setup: skipped -----\";\n        run;\n        %return;\n    %end;\n    %if &_rgrg_state. EQ fail %then %do;\n        %let RAG_PIPELINE_FAILED = 1;\n        %global RAG_JOB_FAILED;\n        %let RAG_JOB_FAILED = 1;\n        /* The message is read with symget and the line is put together in\n           a variable, as the summary below is. Written into the program as\n           a quoted string, a message that took the line beyond 262 bytes\n           made SAS write the NOTE that suspects unbalanced quotation marks\n           above the ERROR. 2000 bytes hold the 500 characters the Python\n           block hands over at most. */\n        data _null_;\n            length message $ 2000 line $ 2100;\n            message = symget(\"_rgrg_error\");\n            line = \"ERROR: RAG - Register Setup failed: \" || message;\n            putLog line;\n        run;\n        /* A run that failed AFTER the score code was stored leaves a model\n           that holds that code. What the code does about TLS certificates\n           is said in this run too, before the session is aborted: on, off\n           and stale are set only once the score code is stored. */\n        %let stored = 0;\n        %if &_rgrg_tlsState. EQ on %then %let stored = 1;\n        %if &_rgrg_tlsState. EQ off %then %let stored = 1;\n        %if &_rgrg_tlsState. EQ stale %then %let stored = 1;\n        %if &stored. EQ 1 %then %do;\n            data _null_;\n                putLog \"WARNING: RAG - Register Setup: the step failed after the score code of the retrieval model was stored. The model in SAS Model Manager holds that score code.\";\n            run;\n        %end;\n        %_rgrg_tls_warnings;\n        %if &RAG_ABORT_ON_ERROR. NE 0 %then %do;\n            data _null_;\n                abort 42;\n            run;\n        %end;\n        %return;\n    %end;\n    /* The summary is read with symget and never written into the program\n       as a quoted string. A summary is usually longer than 262 bytes, and\n       a quoted string of that length makes SAS write the NOTE that suspects\n       unbalanced quotation marks - once for each of the two strings that\n       held it here. 6000 bytes hold the 1500 characters the Python block\n       hands over at most.\n       A part is written as one value with its prefix. Written after the\n       prefix as a value of its own, a part that did not fit into the rest\n       of the line went to the next one without the prefix and left an\n       empty NOTE line behind (seen in a log of RAG - Register Setup). */\n    data _null_;\n        length summary $ 6000 part $ 500 line $ 520;\n        summary = symget(\"_rgrg_summary\");\n        putLog \"NOTE: ----- RAG - Register Setup -----\";\n        do i = 1 to countw(summary, \"|\");\n            part = strip(scan(summary, i, \"|\"));\n            line = \"NOTE:   \" || part;\n            if part ne \"\" then putLog line;\n        end;\n    run;\n    %_rgrg_tls_warnings;\n%mend _rgrg_status;\n%_rgrg_status;"}, "type": "code", "ui": "{\n\t\"showPageContentOnly\": true,\n\t\"pages\": [\n\t\t{\n\t\t\t\"id\": \"pageDefinition\",\n\t\t\t\"type\": \"page\",\n\t\t\t\"label\": \"Definition\",\n\t\t\t\"children\": [\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgrg_info\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"text\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"text\": \"Turns a finished ingestion into a governed, consumable setup: the retrieval model is manifested for THIS collection and registered in SAS Model Manager, the configuration and document manifests are written next to it, and the scheduled ingestion job is generated from your flow so the two cannot drift apart. Run it as the last step of the flow; re-running updates what it created.\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgrg_inventory\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"inputtable\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Load report (from RAG - Load Vector Store):\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgrg_setupName\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"textfield\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Setup name (names the model, the job and the artifact folder):\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"e.g. HR Policies\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": true,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgrg_storeHost\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"textfield\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Vector store host:\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": true,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgrg_storeDb\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"textfield\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Database name:\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": true,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgrg_storeSslmode\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"dropdown\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"SSL mode (allow/prefer/verify-* apply to PostgreSQL; other stores read disable as no TLS and anything else as TLS):\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"items\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"value\": \"disable\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"disable\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"value\": \"allow\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"allow\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"value\": \"prefer\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"prefer\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"value\": \"require\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"require\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"value\": \"verify-ca\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"verify-ca\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"value\": \"verify-full\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"verify-full\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t],\n\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgrg_computeContext\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"textfield\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Compute context for the generated job (must run as the requesting user):\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgrg_flowPath\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"path\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Studio Flow to generate the scheduled job from (optional):\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"pathtype\": \"file\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgrg_sectionAdvanced\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"section\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Runtime\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"open\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"children\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgrg_storePort\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"textfield\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Vector store port (blank = the backend default: 5432 pgvector, 3306 singlestore):\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgrg_credentialDomain\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"textfield\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Credential domain:\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgrg_scrEndpoint\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"textfield\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"SCR base URL of the embedding container (blank = <viya-host>/llm):\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgrg_defaultK\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"numstepper\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Chunks a retrieval returns by default:\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"integer\": true,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"min\": 1,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"max\": null,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"stepsize\": 1,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgrg_sslVerify\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"checkbox\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Verify TLS certificates in the registered retrieval model\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgrg_mmProject\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"textfield\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"SAS Model Manager project:\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgrg_casServer\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"textfield\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"CAS server (for the ledger pointer):\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgrg_contentRoot\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"path\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"SAS Content root of the RAG deployment (set by the deployment - not editable here):\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"pathtype\": \"folder\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"enabled\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"$_rgrg_contentRoot\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"=\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"__set_by_deployment__\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgrg_modelTemplate\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"path\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Retrieval model template (set by the deployment - not editable here):\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"pathtype\": \"file\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"enabled\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"$_rgrg_modelTemplate\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"=\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"__set_by_deployment__\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgrg_ragCorePath\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"path\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"SAS Content folder holding rag_core (set by the deployment - not editable here):\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"pathtype\": \"folder\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"enabled\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"$_rgrg_ragCorePath\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"=\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"__set_by_deployment__\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t]\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgrg_report\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"outputtable\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Registration report output:\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t]\n\t\t},\n\t\t{\n\t\t\t\"id\": \"pageAbout\",\n\t\t\t\"type\": \"page\",\n\t\t\t\"label\": \"About\",\n\t\t\t\"children\": [\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"textAbout\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"text\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"text\": \"RAG - Register Setup step\\n==========\\n\\nThe step that makes an ingestion consumable. It manifests retrieve_context.py with this setup's collection, embedding model, store and corpus version - so no deployed model carries a placeholder - and registers it as a scoreable Model Manager python model with typed variables, stack tags and a trainTable pointer to the ledger. Alongside it go pipeline.yaml, the ingestion manifest (which documents, at which content hash, from which run), the collection manifest and the store DDL a DBA can review. Selecting a Studio Flow also generates the scheduled ingestion job from that flow, carrying a reference back to it, so the scheduled path and the visual path stay the same pipeline. Everything is idempotent: re-registering updates the model, the artifacts and the job definition rather than creating second copies.\\n\\nFlow wiring: chain the document INVENTORY through every step - RAG - List Documents \u2192 Extract Text \u2192 Chunk Documents \u2192 Embed Chunks \u2192 Load Vector Store. The bulk data travels beside the flow in promoted CAS tables named <project>_ELEMENTS, <project>_CHUNKS, <project>_EMBEDDED and <project>_LEDGER in the tables caslib (each saved to disk, so state survives server restarts; names stay within 32 characters so they display nicely in SAS Studio). Each step's output table lands in that same caslib as <project>_INV_LIST, _INV_EXTRACT, _INV_CHUNK, _INV_EMBED and <project>_LOAD_REPORT unless you point the output port somewhere else. Give every step the SAME project name and caslib.\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"sectionPrereqs\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"section\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Pre-requisites\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"open\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"children\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"textPrereqs\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"text\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"text\": \"Tested on SAS Viya 2026 (Stable).\\n\\n* The rag_core runtime must be deployed to SAS Content (default: /SAS Agentic AI Accelerator/RAG/rag_core) with deploy-rag-content.ps1/.sh - keep that folder read-only for regular users.\\n* The compute context's Python needs the requests, swat and pandas packages (swat/pandas carry the pipeline tables to CAS - varchar columns, no 32k limit).\\n* CAS available; the runner needs write access to the tables caslib.\\n* The ingestion must have completed - the load report and the ledger are what this step registers.\\n* Scheduling the generated job stays a separate, deliberate act in SAS Environment Manager.\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t]\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"sectionDocumentation\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"section\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Documentation\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"open\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"children\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"textDocumentation\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"text\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"text\": \"Almost everything is inherited from the inventory: the project, caslib, collection, embedding model, pipeline version, configuration fingerprint and corpus run id all travel with the flow, so only the store connection and the retrieval default are asked for here.\\n\\nVerify TLS certificates in the registered retrieval model (Runtime section, ticked by default) is the default the registered model applies to the two HTTPS calls it makes itself - to the embedding container and to the SAS Viya credentials service. Ticked, the model is manifested with SSL_VERIFY = True and verifies. Unticked, it is manifested with SSL_VERIFY = False and carries the tag TLS-Verification-Off in SAS Model Manager; the log of this step then ends with WARNING lines, and the registration report shows the state in the Detail column of the model row. Unticking is meant for a publishing destination that runs Python where the SAS Viya CA bundle is not mounted - a test system on a closed network, not production. On the destination, RAGEMBED_SSLVERIFY and RAGSTORE_SSLVERIFY set to true or false overrule what was registered. Registering again with the box ticked writes SSL_VERIFY = True and removes the tag.\\n\\nThe WARNING lines describe the model as SAS Model Manager holds it. A run that fails after the score code was stored - the flow named under Studio Flow to generate the scheduled job from does not exist, for example - leaves a model with that score code, so the lines stand in the log of the failing run as well, below its ERROR line. When the upload of the score code gets no usable answer, the step cannot know whether SAS Model Manager stored it: it says so, leaves the tag as it is - the tag may then not say what the stored score code does - and has to be run again.\\n\\nThe setting changes the registered model only. This step itself, the other RAG steps and the ingestion job keep verifying their own calls with the CA bundle of the compute session, and the TLS of the connection to the vector store stays the SSL mode above. If the RAG content was deployed before this setting existed, the retrieval model template has no SSL_VERIFY line: the model then keeps verifying with the box unticked, the step says so in a WARNING, and the RAG content has to be deployed again (deploy-rag-content) before the setting takes effect.\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t]\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"sectionChangelog\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"section\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Changelog\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"open\": true,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"children\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"textChangelog\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"text\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"text\": \"* Version: 1.3 (11OCT2026)\\n      - Checkbox Verify TLS certificates in the registered retrieval model: unticked, the model is manifested with SSL_VERIFY = False and tagged TLS-Verification-Off, the log warns and the registration report shows the state\\n      - A ledger with CHAR columns is read without the blanks CAS pads them with\\n      - A run that fails after the score code was stored still says in its log whether the stored model verifies TLS certificates and whether it carries the tag TLS-Verification-Off; an upload of the score code without a usable answer is reported as not known, with the tag left as it is; a model that cannot be read keeps the tag the listing of the models shows. Where the listing does not show its tags either, the tag is written, and a run whose score code is then not stored says so in a WARNING. That WARNING was not run in SAS with this version of the step\\n      - The model is registered with the variable lengths the Prompt Builder writes (question 32000, filter_json and options 4000, retrieval_mode 32; the outputs as before)\\n      - A ledger (<project>_LEDGER) that was saved but is not in memory - which is how a restart of the CAS server leaves it - is loaded back from its saved file before the step reads it. A saved file that cannot be loaded fails the step. Not run in SAS with this version of the step\\n      - The job generated from a Studio Flow begins with RAG_ABORT_ON_ERROR = 0, so that a failing step does not end the session with abort 42, and ends with a check that writes an ERROR line and sets SYSCC when a step set RAG_JOB_FAILED. Both are added by this step and are not part of the flow: a job that SAS Studio deploys from the flow itself does not have them. Not run in SAS Job Execution with this version of the step\\n      - A step that fails also sets RAG_JOB_FAILED, a flag no step clears. A job that RAG - Register Setup generates from a flow reads it at its end, because RAG_PIPELINE_FAILED is cleared again by a later RAG - List Documents, RAG - Purge Documents or RAG - Retrieve Context of the same flow. Not run in SAS with this version of the step\\n      - The run summary is read with symget, so that a run that succeeds does not write the NOTE about a quoted string of more than 262 bytes above it (measured in SAS Studio for this step). A step that fails can still write the NOTE beside its ERROR line\\n* Version: 1.2 (29JUL2026)\\n      - SAS Content document sources; output tables land in the tables caslib; labelled columns; numeric and list-of-values fields; run summary in the log\\n* Version: 1.1 (28JUL2026)\\n      - Pipeline tables move to promoted CAS tables via SWAT (varchar, no 32k limit); automatic embed checkpoint\\n* Version: 1.0 (28JUL2026)\\n      - Initial version\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t]\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t]\n\t\t}\n\t],\n\t\"syntaxversion\": \"1.3.0\",\n\t\"values\": {\n\t\t\"_rgrg_ragCorePath\": \"/SAS Agentic AI Accelerator/RAG/rag_core\",\n\t\t\"_rgrg_setupName\": \"\",\n\t\t\"_rgrg_storeHost\": \"\",\n\t\t\"_rgrg_storePort\": \"\",\n\t\t\"_rgrg_storeDb\": \"\",\n\t\t\"_rgrg_storeSslmode\": {\n\t\t\t\"value\": \"prefer\",\n\t\t\t\"label\": \"prefer\"\n\t\t},\n\t\t\"_rgrg_credentialDomain\": \"agentic-ai-keys\",\n\t\t\"_rgrg_scrEndpoint\": \"\",\n\t\t\"_rgrg_defaultK\": 4,\n\t\t\"_rgrg_sslVerify\": true,\n\t\t\"_rgrg_mmProject\": \"RAG Engineering\",\n\t\t\"_rgrg_casServer\": \"cas-shared-default\",\n\t\t\"_rgrg_flowPath\": \"\",\n\t\t\"_rgrg_computeContext\": \"SAS Studio compute context\",\n\t\t\"_rgrg_contentRoot\": \"/SAS Agentic AI Accelerator/RAG\",\n\t\t\"_rgrg_modelTemplate\": \"/SAS Agentic AI Accelerator/RAG/models/retrieve_context.py\"\n\t}\n}"}